    {
      "id": "KlEe-4sYeXI6rtFt-3Upo",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -0.37688928212821793,
      "y": -789.3463681516889,
      "width": 715.579345703125,
      "height": 200,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aA",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 235430483,
      "version": 770,
      "versionNonce": 276828562,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "El1PvUIwkeN3fB_YEq35p",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1791306941291,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "a couple starting questions...\n\n[1] how fast does this have to run? we get ~66.5mhz CLK from RP2040\n        [a] does one bit have to be sent in 4 instructions? 8? 1?\n[2] how much data do we have to receive/store at once?\n        [a] how do we say we are \"busy\" or not ready? \n        [b] how fast do we have to send this back to the RP2040/host?\n        [c] how fast are we receiving data from the RP2040/host?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "a couple starting questions...\n\n[1] how fast does this have to run? we get ~66.5mhz CLK from RP2040\n        [a] does one bit have to be sent in 4 instructions? 8? 1?\n[2] how much data do we have to receive/store at once?\n        [a] how do we say we are \"busy\" or not ready? \n        [b] how fast do we have to send this back to the RP2040/host?\n        [c] how fast are we receiving data from the RP2040/host?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "OWl6q2LEzwyN9CNqmde6c",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -10.605111742632516,
      "y": -347.93631267248287,
      "width": 667.5994262695312,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aB",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 468280263,
      "version": 1634,
      "versionNonce": 1004917970,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791306867367,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "a naive starting point...\n\n[1] we will have some connection that in some way gets and sends \n    data from and to a host computer\n[2] the connection will first program Chip 3PO, after which, the chip\n    will be listening for data in (from device and host) and sending\n    in both directions\n[3] the processor onboard will be single-threaded as long as the\n    CLK runs fast enough to poll for signals and send signals \n    while remaining at the desired baud rate",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "a naive starting point...\n\n[1] we will have some connection that in some way gets and sends \n    data from and to a host computer\n[2] the connection will first program Chip 3PO, after which, the chip\n    will be listening for data in (from device and host) and sending\n    in both directions\n[3] the processor onboard will be single-threaded as long as the\n    CLK runs fast enough to poll for signals and send signals \n    while remaining at the desired baud rate",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
