      "index": "ad",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 862068498,
      "version": 696,
      "versionNonce": 1845176974,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1791309233636,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "[1] it seems that 10mbit ethernet will be our toughest challenge...\n    [a] 10mbit = 10,000,000 (10M) bits per second\n    [b] 66mhz = 66,000,000 (66M) cycles per second\n    [c] therefore, we have roughly 6.6 cycles (rounded down to 6)\n        per bit sent; we have to poll and send in 6 instructions\n[2] TLDR; a \"bit-banging\" approach may not work; more may\n    need to be offloaded onto hardware for this to work",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "[1] it seems that 10mbit ethernet will be our toughest challenge...\n    [a] 10mbit = 10,000,000 (10M) bits per second\n    [b] 66mhz = 66,000,000 (66M) cycles per second\n    [c] therefore, we have roughly 6.6 cycles (rounded down to 6)\n        per bit sent; we have to poll and send in 6 instructions\n[2] TLDR; a \"bit-banging\" approach may not work; more may\n    need to be offloaded onto hardware for this to work",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
